HIMS.body:
**HIMS — Huey Internal Messaging System** — is the intended structured messaging and record pathway between bounded components and external controller clients.

Repository foundations exist under `src/huey/messaging` and `src/huey/hims`, including schema, ledger, routing, storage, and related work. This proves a foundation, not a complete authenticated controller service.

## Intended controller functions

- device registration and provisioning;
- device-specific authentication;
- command and request submission;
- acknowledgements and responses;
- operational alerts and structured status;
- reconnection and delivery tracking;
- audit logging;
- key rotation, revocation, replacement, and version reporting.

## Authority rule

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    MESSAGE["Delivered message"] --> AUTHN["Authenticate origin"]
    AUTHN --> VALIDATE["Validate schema and freshness"]
    VALIDATE --> AUTHZ["Authorize requested action"]
    AUTHZ --> CONFIRM["Operator confirmation when required"]
    CONFIRM --> EXECUTE["Bounded execution"]
    EXECUTE --> RECORD["Observed result and log"]
```

A successful delivery does not grant physical execution, identity, governance, or canonical authority.

Huey-Body.body:
**Huey Body is real hardware. It was formerly called Huey Core and is currently paused for the V1 proof.**

Pausing actuation does not abandon embodiment. It separates a useful software proof from unfinished mechanical, electrical, thermal, sensor, and safety integration.

## Body domains

- shell, structure, mounts, and service access;
- sensors and environmental input;
- speakers, displays, lights, and interaction surfaces;
- motors, movement, and other actuators;
- power distribution, charging, battery, and shutdown;
- thermal management;
- hardware interlocks, emergency stop, refusal, and recovery;
- attributable observation of physical results.

## Reactivation gate

Body actuation should return only with a bounded command, authenticated origin, schema and range validation, current-state checks, authorization, operator confirmation where required, power and motion limits, safe-stop, observed result, and a complete record.

The active physical-cohesion program is [[Huey-V4]]. The current V1 proof may complete before V4 is operational.

Collective-and-Bifurcation.body:
## Collective

The Monkey-Head-Project may later coordinate multiple valid Huey nodes. That collective is not presently operational. A shared network, common repository, or pool of accelerators does not by itself create a legitimate collective.

## Bifurcation concepts

| Concept | Intended meaning | Current status |
|---|---|---|
| **Exact bifurcation** | Controlled lineage event preserving a defined base state as faithfully as possible | Provisional concept |
| **Augmented bifurcation** | Controlled divergent or specialized lineage event | Provisional concept |

Neither process automatically determines identity, personhood, citizenship, authority, or governance rights.

## Prerequisites

- one valid local node;
- defined canonical state and export boundary;
- provenance and checksums;
- identity and key management;
- explicit human authorization;
- rollback and revocation;
- conflict and divergence handling;
- governance rules that preserve node boundaries.
